Keep counting past 2^32 numbers in seq.
The count of numbers written was an unsigned int, and each number is
computed as first + n * increment. After 4294967296 numbers the count
wrapped to zero, so seq started over from the first number and never
ended. Make the count 64-bit.

---
 coreutils/seq.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/seq.c
+++ b/coreutils/seq.c
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 		OPT_s = (1 << 1),
 	};
 	double first, last, increment, v;
-	unsigned n;
+	unsigned long long n;
 	unsigned width;
 	unsigned frac_part;
 	const char *sep, *opt_s = "\n";
